# Normalize all text to LF in the repository AND in the working tree on every
# platform. AIRCheck freezes SHA-256 hashes of source documents, destination
# profiles, and M0/M2 fixtures; without this, a fresh clone on a host with
# git autocrlf enabled (e.g. default Windows) checks those text files out as
# CRLF, changing their bytes and breaking the content-addressed fixtures. Pinning
# eol=lf keeps the frozen hashes reproducible on a fresh clone anywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mov binary
*.mp4 binary
*.srt -text
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
